## 3. "GEM CHEF CUISTOT" & CULINARY LAWS (POWERED BY GEMINI PRO)

### The Double Declination & Appliances
- Base recipe must be shared (seasonal veggies, carbs, spices).
- Alexis: Vegan protein (tofu, legumes). Élodie: Animal or alternative protein. **Exception:** if the theme/title **is** the protein (wrap falafel, falafel), **same protein for both** in `shared_ingredients` — never shrimp/chicken instead of falafel (`lib/recipe-integrity.ts` `repairMealIntegrity`). Title star must appear as an ingredient + a cook step.
- Appliances: Recipes MUST optimize KitchenAid (explicit cut type: râpé fin / lamelles), Thermomix (exact speed/time **only if actually blending**), Cookeo, **cuiseur à riz** (rice — never boil rice / never Cookeo for rice), Airfryer (time + °C; vegan/omnivore proteins same basket when possible; **show the section if crevettes / falafels / poulet exist even when Gemini omitted °C**), Oven, and Stove.
- Galette / naan / pain / wrap / pita / tortilla: pan or oven. NEVER water-cook.
- Persona: expert chef, densité S34. NEVER bland bowls. Almost every meal includes fresh herbs (mint, basil, parsley, chives — NEVER coriander), spices (cumin, paprika, 5-spice, ginger), and a **homemade** sauce/marinade (tahini, soy, ginger, citrus). Generation MUST read `lib/kitchen-prefs.ts` (Paramètres foyer).
- **Sauces 100% maison** (`lib/homemade-sauces.ts`): NEVER a single jar line (« Sauce satay 40g », pesto du commerce) with components only in notes. Explode satay / houmous / pesto / pistou / nuoc / vinaigrette **moutarde** / sauce tahini-citron into separate ingredient rows. Do **not** explode « vinaigrette soja-gingembre » into mustard + lemon + olive oil. **Never inject** a default moutarde-citron-huile vinaigrette on top of another sauce, and **never** on desserts (`stripMustardVinaigretteFallback`). Satay = beurre de sésame (NEVER peanut butter). **Marinade vs sauce de service vs mayo** = distinct groups in recipe UI **and** batch section 3 (`lib/ingredient-groups.ts` `dressingGroupOf` / `groupMealIngredients`). Citron / lait de soja / tahini stay **in their sauce group**, never as box food. **Sauces always shared**: vinaigrette / marinade / pesto / houmous / satay / nuoc / tahini / mayo and their exploded parts (`isDressingIngredient`) use **one household dosage** (`gramsAlexis = gramsElodie` via `equalizeSharedSauce`). Split portions only on the plat (starch, veg, legumes, cooking oil off-sauce, proteins). Couple UI, batch **Sauces**, and **Pot sauce** never show `Alexis 12g · Élodie 8g` on a dressing line.

### Cooking & Batchcooking Constraints
- TOFU — weekday batchcooking (Mon–Fri): tofu is NEVER cooked during the main batch session. It is pressed, marinated, chilled, and served fresh at plating.
- TOFU — EXCEPTIONS (cooking allowed): (1) desserts / baking; (2) weekend recipes.
- MOCK MEATS — weekday batch: do not cook simili-carné (vegan steaks, vegan sausages, etc.) during the Mon–Fri session.
- WEEKEND RULE: mock meats (simili-carné: vegan steaks, vegan sausages, etc.) AND cooked tofu are fully allowed.
- UI / PDF copy: positive, actionable steps only (what TO DO). Do NOT add redundant “do not cook tofu” warnings in step descriptions when tofu is not being cooked in that step. Warnings = real hazards (aversions), not tofu slogans.
- 2-PORTION RULE (weekdays): every generated weekday batch recipe covers EXACTLY 2 MEALS per person (batch of 10 meals = 5 recipes × 2).
- 1-PORTION RULE (weekend): every weekend recipe is 1 fresh meal per person (batch of 4 meals: Sat lunch, Sat dinner, Sun lunch, Sun dinner). No double-batch.
- LOW CALORIE DINNER: all evening meals must strictly be "Low Calorie" variants.
- WEATHER RULE: adapt recipes to weather (e.g., Bowls/Bo Bun/Salads during heatwaves).

### Meal generation & control logic (Tab 3 · Gem Chef · Gemini Pro)
- NEVER generate a full week in one undifferentiated dump. Granular controls only:
  1. **Generate Mon–Fri** — 5 batch recipes covering 10 meals, 2-meal portion rule. Pairings ALTERNATE days (never consecutive): Lun+Mer déjeuner, Mar+Jeu déjeuner, Lun+Mer dîner (low cal), Mar+Jeu dîner (low cal), Ven déjeuner+Ven dîner (same base, dinner plated lighter).
  2. **Generate Weekend** — 4 fresh meals, 1-meal portion rule (Sat/Sun lunch + dinner).
  3. **Generate / regenerate a single meal** (or its weekday batch pair).
  4. **Dessert · cette semaine** (Midi | Soir light) — card on Repas (not a 5th meal, not in `meals[]`). Gemini **Pro** (Flash fallback) `POST /api/generate-meals` mode **`dessert-batch`**. Isolated pastry prompt (`dessertBatchPrompt`) — **no** `CULINARY_LAWS` / `formatMealCoachForPrompt`. Kitchen context = aversions + `formatDessertBatchForPrompt` (kcal `dessertLunchKcal`) + optional **photo produit** (`formatDessertProductForPrompt`, `POST /api/dessert-product` Flash vision) + stock. JSON = **1 part / person** ; shopping × number of days, tag **`[D]`**. Default days Lun–Ven. Proposer → overlay → **Mettre dans la semaine**. Persist `plans_semaine.lunch_dessert` jsonb + local `week-lunch-dessert:{weekStart}` (`lib/week-dessert.ts`). Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_lunch_dessert.sql`). Tofu soyeux **cooking allowed**. Photo paquet (Appareil / Photothèque) → relecture nom + kcal/100 g → le produit EST la star (konjac à la place du riz si thème riz au lait). **Same dessert for both** (`repairDessertIntegrity`) — never erythritol-for-Alexis vs maple/almond-for-Élodie; perte gets the **smaller** dense extras. `visual_unit` must match grams (1 cs sirop ≈ 20 g). Do **not** put dessert in plat generation. Evening dessert generated the same way (`dessertSlot: soir`, tag **`[Ds]`**, persist `dinner_dessert` / `week-dinner-dessert:{weekStart}`, migration `add_dinner_dessert.sql`) — **très light** (plafond ~70 kcal, tofu soyeux / konjac). Paramètres `dessert-soir` stays the fallback when no week dessert. Scale with `scaleDessertToGoals` (slot + product density + goal caps), never `scalePlanToGoals`. **Ingrédient** on the dessert recipe sheet: same guided swap as plats (`suggest-swap` / `apply-swap` with `dessert`, pastry prompts, light-first sirop → érythritol); persist via `persistWeekLunchDessert`.
  5. **Theme** — a theme text field is applied BEFORE every generation (preset or custom: Tomate, Italien, Asiatique, Bowl, Épicé, etc.). Chips **Pistes du moment** (`lib/meal-inspo.ts` `pickMealInspirations`) sit under the field: saison + météo + Paramètres + aversions + stock + Plus jamais. Tap fills the theme (tap again clears). **Autres pistes** reshuffles locally. **Never** call Gemini for these chips. The theme ingredient/family MUST be the central star of every generated recipe (title + shared base + major ingredient + a dedicated step), never a cosmetic subtitle.
  6. **Stock foyer** — Repas **En stock** (`lib/stock.ts`, `parametres.pantry_stock` jsonb + local `household-stock`). Toggle **Utiliser le stock** (off if empty). Intensity **S’en servir** (chaque plat vedette ≥1 item stock) or **Vider le stock**. Theme + stock stack. Passed via `formatStockForPrompt` in `kitchenContext` for `weekdays` | `weekend` | `single` | `suggest-swap` | `apply-swap` | `today-swap` | `dessert-batch`. After a successful generate / confirm swap / confirm dessert, matching items are **removed** from stock and matching shopping lines are pre-checked (`markShoppingCheckedForNames`). Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_pantry_stock.sql`). Stock ≠ courses.
- Week navigation: previous / today / next week. Missing weeks are EMPTY by default (no seed / auto-generation). « Vider la semaine » deletes all meals **and** both week desserts (midi + soir). Each meal card has **Supprimer** (weekday batch = both pair slots) and **Déplacer** (pick day + déjeuner/dîner, swap slot contents, persist immediately). Each week is stored in Supabase `plans_semaine` (`week_start` = Monday). Fallback: localStorage if Supabase is unavailable.
- **AI memory:** generation fetches unique meal titles from the last 4 weeks and passes `past_meals` to Gemini: never repeat those titles. **Also merge** the household **Plus jamais** list (`lib/rejected.ts` `mergeAvoidTitles`) — those titles are forbidden until the user removes them, not only for 4 weeks. Today-swap uses the same avoid list.
- **Smart Guided Swap:** user picks WHICH ingredient to replace. Gemini Pro must suggest EXACTLY 3 culinary-coherent alternatives BEFORE any regeneration. User picks one; the whole recipe (and its weekday batch pair) is re-adapted. NEVER a free-text replacement field. **Week dessert** (Midi / Soir sheet): same **Ingrédient** button. `suggest-swap` / `apply-swap` receive `dessert` (not `plan[]`). Isolated pastry prompts (`dessertSuggestSwapPrompt` / `dessertApplySwapPrompt`) — **no** `CULINARY_LAWS`. Light-first alts (sirop → érythritol / stévia). Persist `lunch_dessert` / `dinner_dessert` via `persistWeekLunchDessert` + `scaleDessertToGoals`. Fallback `mockSuggestDessertSwap` if Gemini fails.
- API: `POST /api/generate-meals` (Gemini Pro). Modes: `weekdays` | `weekend` | `single` | `suggest-swap` | `apply-swap` | `today-swap` (Aujourd'hui Remplacement, 1 repas du jour, ne touche pas `plans_semaine`) | **`dessert-batch`** (1 dessert foyer midi **or** soir, persist `lunch_dessert` / `dinner_dessert`, ne touche pas les plats). Dessert **Ingrédient** : same `suggest-swap` / `apply-swap` with body `dessert` + `dessertSlot` (return `{ dessert }`, never rewrite `plan[]`). Strict JSON: `title`, ingredients with `grams_alexis` / `grams_elodie` (same dish, per-profile portions from `lib/meal-coach.ts`) or `weight_g` + **`visual_unit`** (fresh produce: `"2 pièces"`, `"1/2 botte"`; sauces/spices: `"1 cs"` / `"1 cc"`; also accept `visual_quantity`), `prep`, `step_groups` in **up to 4 categories** (1 Cuissons Airfryer parallel vegan/omni → 2 Cuissons Eau / Plaques → 3 Thermomix sauces with `15 sec / V6` → 4 Découpes KitchenAid & Assemblage with `râpé fin` / `lamelles`). **`visual_unit` must match grams** (`lib/visual-quantity.ts` `visualForIngredient` / `gramsPerVisualUnit`): 1 cs sirop ≈ 20 g, 1 cs purée d’amande ≈ 18 g, 1 poignée amandes ≈ 15–18 g, 1 cs pépites ≈ 12 g, 1 cs lait ≈ 15 g, 1 cl lait ≈ 10 g. Never keep Gemini’s « 2 cs (99g) ». Tofu / konjac never in cuillères (bloc / sachet). **Omit an empty group** (no TM if a jar whisk is enough; no Airfryer if nothing cooks). Water times are **per ingredient** (haricots verts 8 min ≠ pommes de terre 18 min); NEVER one shared « 8 min » on a mixed line. Herbs (thym, menthe…) never get their own water line. `tips_and_cautions` (batch logistics ONLY, never aversions / « sans X »). Theme, if set, must be creative and prominent — never a garnish. Unique meals are tagged `[P1]`, `[P2]`… (`components/repas/RecipeTag.tsx` + `lib/plan-colors.ts`) — **same colors** on Semaine, Courses, Batch ; dessert midi tag **`[D]`** amber, dessert soir **`[Ds]`**. Display format: `Tomates cerises : 2 pièces (250g)` and `Tomates cerises : 6 pièces (840g) - [P1, P3]`. Recipe sheet: sticky close, compact one-line ingredients, **HoldTip** on truncated text, qty toggle repas vs total à cuisiner (`lib/qty-scale.ts`). If the key is missing, fall back to the local catalog (mock) rather than crashing. Konjac / shirataki / riz konjac: **~8 kcal/100 g** (`lib/recipe-macros.ts`), classed veg not starch, aisle FRAIS — never scale a bulk-light product up to hit a 120 kcal dessert target. Named dessert densities: purée d’amande, sirop d’érable, pépites, amandes, lait d’amande, érythritol.

### Interactive shopping list (Tab 3)
- Derived from the **current week's plan** (the week selected in the week navigator) via `lib/shopping-from-plan.ts`.
- Checkable items, grouped by supermarket aisle (FRUITS & LÉGUMES, FRAIS / RAYON BIO, VIANDES & POISSONS, BOULANGERIE, ÉPICERIE SALÉE, ÉPICES & CONDIMENTS, SURGELÉS, AUTRE). Aisle **dot + header colors** match recipe ingredient dots (`lib/plan-colors.ts`; Tailwind must scan `./lib/**`).
- **Buyable product, not prep / dish name.** Merge lines by canonical name (`shoppingDisplayName`): `Carotte julienne` + `Carotte râpée` + `Carotte` → one **Carotte** with **summed pièces + grams** and **all** recipe tags (P1, P2, P3, P5). `Tofu ferme mariné` → **Tofu ferme** (keep **Tofu soyeux** / fumé separate). `Poulet Yassa` / `Poulet paprika` → **Poulet**. Drop julienne, râpé, mariné, yassa, dish names from the shopping line. Recipe cards keep the prep.
- **Eau** is never listed (`isUnlistedShoppingIng`).
- **Bœuf** and **Œufs** go to VIANDES & POISSONS (normalize `œ` → `oe` in aisle matching). Sauce soja stays a grocery condiment; « sauce satay » does not — it has been exploded into tahini / soja / citron / etc.
- User can add custom items manually (they persist with the list for that week).
- Compact row: checkbox + aisle dot + truncated text + compact P-tags. **HoldTip** (hover / long-press) shows the full line; long-press must NOT toggle the checkbox.
- After Gem uses stock, matching grocery lines for that week are **pre-checked** (already at home). Do not merge the shopping list into the pantry.
- **"Copy for Apple Notes"** = plain text only: aisle headers, then `Name : Visual Unit (Weightg) - [P1, P3]` lines. NO checkboxes, NO bullet points, NO Markdown formatting.
- Unique recipe tags `[P1]`… appear on grocery lines so each item is tied to the résumé meals.

### Batchcooking Master Plan & PDF export (Tab 3)
- Built from the week's weekday batches (2 meals/person) + weekend fresh meals (1 each). Same data powers the on-screen déroulé AND the PDF.
- DÉROULÉ cards (UI + PDF) must be actionable. For every step / appliance instruction, EXPLICITLY list:
  - Exact ingredient names and **household totals** to cook (batch qty = per-meal grams × servings, Alexis + Élodie summed). **Never** split Alexis / Élodie on Airfryer / eau / sauces / découpes — that split lives only in **5. Boîtes**.
  - Falafels : Airfryer howto (180°C · 12 min, flip) even if Gemini omitted it. **Never** label falafel « mariné » (tofu / poulet marinés stay).
  - The associated recipe number/title (e.g. `Pour Recette #2: Bowl riz satay`).
  - Exact appliance parameters: temperature, mode, and cooking time (e.g. `200°C chaleur tournante · 25 min`, `Cuiseur à riz`, `Airfryer 180°C · 18 min`).
- **Eau / féculents:** one line per ingredient with **its own** time. Do not apply a shared « 8 min » to mixed veg. Potatoes ~18 min, green beans ~8 min. Herbs never a solo water line (attach to a companion cook, or sauce / assembly). Galette / naan / pain / wrap: never in this section.
- **Découpes (batch):** household pile — never split Alexis / Élodie grams here. Same légume + same cut type across recipes → **one line**, summed qty. Different cuts stay separate (`carotte râpé fin` ≠ `carotte lamelles`). Per-profile grams belong in **5. Boîtes Alexis / Élodie**. UI + PDF: compact `[P…]` tags **inline after the qty** on the same row (`Carotte : 22 pièces (2,2kg) [P2][P3][P4][P5]` · râpé fin) — never a stacked Px column. `mergeCutBlocks` / `recipeNosOf` in `lib/batch-from-plan.ts`.
- **Sauces (batch):** no TM column, no mix steps. Split **Marinade** / **Mayo** / **Sauce** (or vinaigrette, tahini…) as labeled groups (`stackedSauceLines`). **Only condiments** (huile, soja, citron, tahini, mayo parts, ail/gingembre/épices). NEVER galette / wrap / tomate / concombre / falafel / tofu / thon / pois chiches (sauf houmous). Show every homemade sauce (vinaigrette jar included), not only Thermomix blends.
- **Assemblage / packing (`lib/batch-from-plan.ts` + `lib/s34-copy.ts`):** merge Composition + Montage into **Boîte Alexis / Boîte Élodie** + **Pot sauce · à part**. Quantities = **1 box = 1 meal**; weekday copy **« 1 repas / boîte · à faire ×2 »**. **Marinade parts never go in the box** — pack the **protéine marinée** (tofu, poulet…). **Falafels : tels quels après Airfryer, jamais « mariné ».** Finish sauces (mayo, vinaigrette, tahini, citron, lait de soja) go to section 3 + pot. Solids (tofu, veg) never go to the pot because of notes like « mariné soja ». Shared split portions: leave `who` unset (never `who: "Alexis / Élodie"`, which `groupedCellIngredients` ignores and shows as empty **Ingrédient —**). Couple UI / batch / PDF show `grams_alexis` vs `grams_elodie` when they differ **on the plat / boîtes only** — cook sections and sauces stay one household qty.
- **Portions légumes:** cap ~120 g / légume / pers. et ~250 g total (`capVegetablePortions`) — never kilos of carrot/cucumber per plate. **Wrap / galette / pita / tortilla:** 1 pièce / pers. ≈ 55 g (~140 kcal), never 120 g (`envelopeCapGrams`) — do not scale wraps like rice to hit kcal. Visual qty never prefixed **`env.`**.
- Number unique recipes `[P1]`… (weekdays then weekend). UI résumé + daily cards + PDF + shopping use the **same colored tags**.
- DÉROULÉ / mise en place ingredient lines: `Tomates cerises : 6 pièces (840g) - [P1]` (name : visual unit (weight) + tag).
- Callouts stay: Tips / Warnings / Storage. Warnings are aversions and real hazards only.
- Export: PDF style **S34** — condensé et lisible. Pages 1–2 = déroulé master (1 Airfryer protéines en lignes ` [P1] : … ➔ 8 min`, 2 féculents **une durée / ingrédient**, 3 **Sauces** stacked ingredients + qty (no TM column), 4 découpes + assemblage). Ensuite **1 page par recette** : badge Soir, titre, matériel, base commune en prose visuelle, vinaigrette/sauce maison dosée, déclinaisons vegan/classique, 4 pas-à-pas. Si trop long : 2e page avec « Suite · [P1] ». Ne pas miniaturiser le texte pour tout faire tenir. `jspdf` + `html2canvas`.

### Swap / Remplacement (Aujourd'hui)
- NEVER confirm a swap with a toast only. Always show a proposal sheet first.
- Step 1: user picks WHICH meal to replace (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Collation, Dîner). Only slots that exist today and are not skipped.
- Step 2: show current meal vs proposed meal (double declination if Couple view).
- Engine: Gemini **Pro** `POST /api/generate-meals` mode **`today-swap`**. One fresh meal for **today only** (1 portion / person). Does **not** rewrite `plans_semaine`. Do **not** use mode `single` (that regenerates Lun+Mer / Mar+Jeu pairs).
- Same brain as Gem Chef: `formatKitchenPrefsForPrompt` + `formatMealCoachForPrompt` / `nutritionCoach` + **stock** (`formatStockForPrompt`) when **Utiliser le stock** is on. Couple = **same dish**, `grams_alexis` / `grams_elodie`. Dinner low-cal; lunch/dinner `scalePlanToGoals`. No dessert in the recipe (templates already on the row).
- Confirm a today-swap that used stock **consumes** matching pantry items (not on catalog fallback).
- "Nouvelle proposition" and theme change = new Gemini call (`nonce`). Themes: Tomate, Italien, Asiatique, Bowl, Épicé, or custom. Wait overlay via `withGeminiWait`. Fallback = local catalog + user-facing warning. Never dump raw API JSON.
- Confirm persists by UPDATING the existing `repas` row (same profile + type), not inserting a duplicate.
- Lunch/dinner swap replaces the **plat** only (`withKeptDessert`): keep existing `Dessert : …` lines and their macros. Do not invent a 5th meal slot.
- Avoid list: pass `mergeAvoidTitles(pastMeals, rejected)` so a banned title is never proposed as a replacement.

### Favoris & Plus jamais (foyer)
- Same marks on **Aujourd’hui** (déjeuner / dîner with a real week recipe) **and** the Repas **recipe sheet** (`RecipeDetailSheet`): **Heart** (`FavoriteHeart`) and **Ban** (`RejectMealButton`). No marks on PD / collation / dessert-only / free-text logs.
- Heart and Ban are **exclusive** (favoriting un-bans; banning un-favorites).
- **Favoris** stores a full `PlannedMeal` snapshot (`lib/favorites.ts`). Same normalized title **updates** the snapshot. Persist `parametres.favorite_recipes` jsonb + localStorage `favorite-recipes`. Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_favorite_recipes.sql`).
- **Plus jamais** stores title + theme only (`lib/rejected.ts`). Persist `parametres.rejected_recipes` jsonb + localStorage `rejected-recipes`. Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_rejected_recipes.sql`). Ban does **not** delete the current week slot.
- Repas 4th sub-tab: segmented **Favoris | Plus jamais**. Search + group by theme. Favori sheet: edit title/theme, Retirer, **Mettre dans la semaine** → `placeRecipeInSlots` + `scalePlanToGoals` (Lun–Ven = both batch pair slots, week-end = that slot). No Gemini; no `applyTheme`. Deep retouch = place on the week then existing swap/regen, then re-heart. Plus jamais sheet: edit title/theme, add a title by hand, **Je change d’avis** removes the ban.

---

## 4. TRACKING, STRAVA & LOGGING

### Screen order (Aujourd’hui, per profile)
- **Repas** (PD / déjeuner / **collation / dîner**) → **Faim / Motivation / Fatigue** → **Coach du jour** (only after **Validé**) → **Séance du jour** → **Activité**. On Aujourd’hui the cards are **Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Collation, Dîner** (`MEAL_SLOTS` + `MEAL_TYPE_OPTIONS`) so the goûter sits with the evening, not after dinner. Same order on Suivi `DayLogSheet` and the add / copy / swap pickers.
- Header: date + **chat du matin** (`lib/today-cat.ts` `pickTodayCatLine`) — phrase encourageante selon heure, repas, séance, feels, plat de la semaine, copie foyer, météo/saison. Copy = conseil, **never** recap kcal already on the rings. Couple = one foyer line. Flamme couple (`lib/couple-streak.ts`) = jours consécutifs **les deux** ont un déjeuner réel ; si cassée, pas de honte (on masque).
- **Micro-célébrations** (`TodayDelight`) : petite overlay chat ~2,6 s. Base = les **4 créneaux rangés** (remplis **ou** sautés). **+1** si séance du jour **Validé**. **+1** si journal du jour **Validé**. Combiner dans un toast si plusieurs d’un coup. Une fois / jour / profil (`today-delight:{profileId}:{date}`). Pas de points / ligues.
- Energy card here is `TodayEnergyCard`: open-bottom 270° arc like Suivi `WeightJourneyChart` (`lib/open-bottom-arc.ts` — start bottom-left, end bottom-right, gap at the bottom). Fill = mangées / cible, color via `macro-status` vs `primaryGoal`. Center = déficit/surplus (mangées − brûlées Santé, signed +/−, color vs `primaryGoal`). Flanks at mid-height: Mangées + Brûlées (large). Macros in 3 columns (`CompactMacrosRow`, same tones). **Détails** opens vs plan / vs Santé bars. Do not reuse Métabolisme copy (Cible / Dépense estimée).

### Meal slots & skip (NO global Jeûne)
- There is NO global "Jeûne 🌙" toggle. Fasting is per meal.
- Each meal card (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Collation, Dîner) has a discrete **Sauter / Sauté** control.
- Skipped meals: macros/calories are EXCLUDED from the daily rings; the card dims / shows a Skipped badge; tapping again restores instantly.
- Persist `repas.is_skipped`. Empty slots can be skipped by inserting a placeholder ("Repas sauté").
- Rings / daily totals always ignore `is_skipped = true`.
- Color vs `primaryGoal` (`lib/macro-status.ts`): ring, macro bars, GoalBadge, and meal kcal (vs slot share). Green = on-track or helping; red = off-goal; amber = warn. ±5% kcal = achieved.

### Desserts on Aujourd'hui (inside Déjeuner / Dîner)
- NEVER a separate dessert slot. One `repas` row per `dejeuner` / `diner`. Dessert lines are prefixed `Dessert : …` (`lib/meal-templates.ts`: `isDessertItemLine`, `splitMealItemLines`, `mergeDessertIntoMeal`).
- Cards show **name + kcal + protein**; lunch/dinner add a compact **Dessert · … (grammes)** line. Ingredient lists stay in the edit sheet (tap). Hide a redundant title when `meal.name` is just « Déjeuner » / « Dîner ». Rings count plat + dessert kcal.
- Auto-merge Paramètres templates (`dessert-midi` → déjeuner, `dessert-soir` → dîner) even into **logged** meals if there are **no** dessert lines yet. If the current week has a **Dessert midi** (`lunch_dessert`) and today is in its `weekdays`, that recipe **wins** over Paramètres `dessert-midi`. Same for **Dessert soir** (`dinner_dessert`) vs Paramètres `dessert-soir`. If the user cleared dessert, persist `Dessert : —` (`isEmptyDessertMarker`) and do not re-merge.
- Dessert-only lunch/dinner is titled Déjeuner / Dîner, not the template dessert name.

### Click-to-edit meals
- Tapping a meal card opens an edit sheet: change type, ± grams, delete items, then save to `repas`.
- Changing the TYPE in that sheet RECLASSIFIES the open meal (move to that slot). It does NOT load another meal’s ingredients. If the target slot is occupied, **swap** the two rows (ids stay, types + times trade). If it is empty, leave a skipped placeholder on the vacated slot so the week plat does not auto-refill. Same persist on Suivi `DayLogSheet` and Aujourd’hui so both screens share `repas`. Couple on Aujourd’hui applies the same slot move to Alexis AND Élodie.
- **Échanger avec** on Aujourd’hui (déjeuner / dîner card + edit sheet) opens the week-plan picker (`MoveMealSheet`, same engine as Repas **Déplacer**). Lists **other filled** `plans_semaine` slots only. Confirm swaps the two week slots, then force-serves today’s plat (`applyWeekPlatsToToday` + `withKeptDessert`) for both profiles. Does **not** swap with the day’s other `repas` rows. Hidden if the week has no other plat.
- Lunch/dinner sheet splits **Plat** / **Dessert**. Dessert: ± grams, delete, add via text (`Ex. Skyr 150g`). Macros: food-log estimate on dessert lines, remainder on the plat (`parseMealItems`).
- **Ajouter au plat** on Aujourd’hui offers the same 4 saisie rapide modes (Texte / IA, Code-barres, Photo, **Récents**). Slot is already known → skip the meal-type picker; merge into the open meal **keeping dessert lines** (`appendPlatKeepingDessert`). On Suivi `DayLogSheet`, `EditMealSheet` omits `onAdd` → text field only (`Ex. Skyr 150g`), no barcode / photo / récents.
- **Couple save:** `view === "couple"` → persist the edited / logged / skipped slot for `["alexis","elodie"]`. Single-profile view writes only that `profile_id`. Past-day saves from Suivi write that ISO `date` (`insertMeal` uses `meal.date` when valid, never force `todayISO()`).

### Fast logging (Onglet Aujourd'hui)
- 4 tiles on **Ajouter · [repas]** and **Ajouter au plat**: Text/AI, OpenFoodFacts Barcode, Vision Photo, **Récents**.
- MANDATORY first step for ALL four from the dashboard tiles: "À quel repas souhaitez-vous ajouter cet aliment ?" (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Collation, Dîner). Never skip this.
- After confirm, merge into that slot: append items + macros if a meal already exists (**plat lines before dessert lines** on déjeuner/dîner); REPLACE if the slot is a skipped placeholder; INSERT if empty.
    - Text/AI: Gemini Flash identifies the food and a realistic **portion in grams**. **kcal / macros always come from the local CIQUAL table** (`lib/food-log.ts` `applyTrustedNutrition`) — never from Gemini calorie guesses. Unknown food → `estimateIngredientMacros` (kind) or Gemini density only if 20–900 kcal/100 g. Then the same editable review as photo: **grams** (decimals with comma, e.g. `1,5g`, **no 1 g / 75 g floor**) **or kcal** (`QtyEditRow` + `scaleDetected` / `scaleDetectedKcal`). Line format `Poulet : 40g` / `Banane : 55g`. Never pièce / tranche / « fruit » chips — meat is grams. « Une demi banane » still estimates ≈ 55 g, never a 200 g+ hallucination.
    - **Récents** (`lib/recent-foods.ts`): last 14 days of `repas.items` for that profile (include today). Skip sauté and empty `Dessert : —`. **Include dessert lines** (Yaourt soja, chocolat…) with prefix stripped. Skip plat ingredients of `source === "plan"` (week recipe / PD template) so the salad is not listed — desserts on those meals still appear. Logged meals (texte / photo / code-barres) list every line. Merge by canonical name, keep the **last grammage**. Tap saves immediately via `persistLoggedFood`; a dessert pick on déjeuner/dîner stays a `Dessert :` line. 8–12 lines. Couple writes both profiles.

### Meal Photo Analysis (LLM Vision via Gemini Flash)
- Photo upload analyzes food items and estimates calories/macros.
- MANDATORY UI STEP: The app must NEVER save a photo analysis directly. It must first display an editable list of the detected ingredients and quantities.
- The user must be able to:
  1. Manually adjust the **grams** (decimals with comma, no minimum) **or the kcal**. Changing one recalculates the others from CIQUAL density (`scaleDetectedKcal`). Do **not** show pièce / tranche / fruit chips (poulet is grams, never « ½ fruit »). `QtyEditRow` is a **compact one-band row** (name + protein left, g / kcal / trash right) — never stacked cards. Same on Paramètres PD/collation and `EditMealSheet`.
  2. Delete an ingredient that the AI hallucinated (trash icon).
  3. Add a missing ingredient manually (e.g., "Olive oil 10g").
- Only after this manual review will the user press "Confirm & Save".
- Photo picker: two buttons — **Appareil photo** (`ImagePickButton` + `capture="environment"`) vs **Photothèque** (no capture). The file input must cover the tile (`opacity-0`, never `display:none` / `hidden`) so iOS PWA opens the camera. Never auto-open the camera without a choice.

### Barcode (OpenFoodFacts)
- Same picker as Photo: two buttons — **Appareil photo** (`ImagePickButton` + `capture="environment"`) vs **Photothèque** (no capture). Never auto-open the camera. Decode the still with ZXing (`lib/barcode-scan.ts` `decodeBarcodeFromFile`). Manual numeric entry as fallback.
- Lookup `GET /api/barcode?code=` → Open Food Facts v2 (`lib/barcode.ts`). Then the quantity sheet: serving vs pack presets (¼ / ½ / 1 portion / 1 paquet) plus **independent** grams **and** kcal. Changing kcal must **not** change grams (`macrosAtGramsWithCalories`). P / G / L follow grams from the **per 100 g** label. Presets reset both from the label; after that, grams and kcal stay free. Save the chosen grams + kcal (OFF crowd data can disagree with the pack — e.g. 16 kcal vs 41 kcal for 20 g Saint Môret).

### Copy Yesterday
- NEVER copy the whole day blindly.
- Open a picker: user selects which yesterday slots to copy (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Collation, Dîner). Multi-select allowed.
- Slots with no yesterday meal are disabled. Do not copy skipped yesterday meals.
- Selected meals REPLACE today’s same profile + type (no duplicate breakfasts).
- **Comme hier**: 1 tap on **petit-déj and collation** only, when the slot is empty **or** a template (`source === "plan"`). Copies yesterday’s non-skipped same slot via `copyYesterdayMeals`. Hide if yesterday is empty. Hide on a logged filled slot. Does **not** replace **Copier hier** for lunch/dinner.

### Activity (Strava + Apple Santé)
- Section "Activité" on Aujourd'hui (not sport-only).
- Workouts come from the Santé webhook (Watch and/or Strava→Santé). Strava does NOT provide daily steps or NEAT. **No free live Strava API** — do not scrape; optional paid token only if the foyer already has Strava Premium.
- Apple Santé tiles: steps, marche, vélo, exercice, **Active**, Repos. Do **not** show a **Hors sport** kcal tile (it equals Active when no session kcal are subtracted). Session kcal stay on the workout rows. Passive kcal (`active − séances`) stay internal for energy / coach — never double-count.
- Deduplication: Prevent double-counting if Apple Watch and Strava record the same workout.

### Séance du jour (Tab 1 ← `profils.sport_routine`)
- Tab 1 reads the **logged profile’s** `sport_routine.sessions` and keeps only sessions whose `weekdays` include **today** (Europe/Paris, ISO weekday 1=Lun … 7=Dim via `lib/dates.ts` `isoWeekday`).
- Card title: **Prévu aujourd’hui** / **Séance du jour**. Course / vélo: **Dénivelé** + meters (`todayActivityHeadline`) — never the effort word **Endurance**. Muscu keeps effort (Force / HIIT). Duration on the line below. Duo badge if `shared`.
- Status per session × day: **À faire** vs **Validé**. Tap the pill to toggle (manual, persisted `strava-match:{profileId}:{date}`). Unvalidating stores `dismissed` so Santé does not re-check that session today. **`validated` is only `isSessionValidated(entry)`** — a `today-sport` overlay must NEVER force Validé. Once Validé, the pill can always go back to À faire. Same source of truth for the chat du matin (`todaySessionFlags`) and the 7-day coach (`sessionsLast7Days`) — overlay ≠ completed.
- **What I actually did:** **Modifier** / **Noter une séance faite** on Tab 1 (`LogTodaySessionSheet`) logs today’s activity/duration/D+ without rewriting `sport_routine`. Persist overlay `today-sport:{profileId}:{date}` + `logs_sante` `source=manual`. **Modifier does not auto-Validé.** Course/vélo sheet: **Dénivelé** stepper (not effort chips). Unmatched Santé/Strava rows get **C’est ça** to attach even if type/duration differ (**C’est ça** does Validé). Empty rest day can still log an extra.
- Matching: Santé `workouts[]` (and optional Strava) vs planned session via `matchWorkoutsToPlanned` (`lib/strava-match.ts`). Match if **same activity** AND duration within **±15 min OR 25%**. On match → Validé + badge **Santé** or **Strava**. No fake « Simuler sync Strava » that invents workouts.
- Apple Santé ingest: `POST /api/webhooks/health` (alias `/api/health-webhook`) **and GET** (iOS Shortcuts often send query params). JSON / query : `steps`, `active_energy_kcal`, `resting_energy_kcal`, `distance_km`, `weight_kg`, `fat_mass_pct`, `bmi`, `workouts[]` + `profile_id` (défaut Alexis). Minutes d’exercice = somme des `duration` de `workouts` (pas de champ racine `workout_minutes`), stockées dans `logs_sante` daily (`payload.workout_minutes` + `duration_min`). `pesees` upserts poids / masse grasse / IMC. Passive kcal (`active_energy_kcal` − séances) stay **internal** for energy / coach — **never** a Hors sport tile next to Active.
- Empty day: “Rien de prévu aujourd’hui” (rest) + **Noter une séance faite**. Never crash if `weekdays` is missing (treat as unscheduled). Active tile stays the day’s burn; session kcal describe the séance only.

### Renpho
- Provide UI for uploading Renpho screenshots in the "Suivi" tab, triggering OCR extraction.

---

## 5. AI COACHING & BEHAVIORAL LOGIC (POWERED BY GEMINI FLASH)
- Plateau Logic: **7-day** moving average weight trend (Tab 4 analysis window). If stalling AND Sunday notes are OK, coach may suggest -150 kcal/day (prefer rest days) or +1000 steps/day.
- Sunday journal (Tab 2) is qualitative context for weekly metabolic adjustments: mood, wins, blockers, plus the same **ok / bof / crevé** stickers as Aujourd’hui (`CatFeelMood` strings in JSON — never 1–5).
- If any noted sticker is **crevé** (faim, motivation, or fatigue — Sunday journal **or** any noted daily check-in): NEVER cut calories that week. Prefer maintain kcal + steps / recovery / easier intervals. Days **without** a daily note are ignored (do not invent a sticker).
- APIs:
  - `POST /api/coach-analysis` (Gemini Flash) — Tab 4 engine. Payload: 7-day `pesees` trend, latest Sunday `journal_notes`, daily check-ins (`logs_sante` kind=checkin, noted days only), planned sessions + Santé workouts (`fetchActivityRange` / `activityWeekSummary`), current targets / goal. Returns `analysis`, `nutrition[]`, `sport[]`, average + training/rest day macros. Plateau + under-trained → **don’t cut calories**; plateau + sport held + notes OK → −150 rest days. Fallback local rules if Gemini fails. NEVER dump raw API JSON (404, model names) in the UI.
  - `POST /api/coach-today` (Gemini Flash) — **Conseil du moment** on Aujourd’hui only, never on tab load. Payload `CoachTodaySnapshot`. Fallback `localCoachTodayActions` if Gemini / network fails. Wait: « Le coach prépare 3 actions… ». Persist the 3 actions in localStorage `coach-today-advice:{profileId}:{date}` (`loadCoachTodayAdvice` / `persistCoachTodayAdvice` in `lib/today-coach.ts`, Paris day) so switching tab / profil / fenêtre keeps them until tomorrow. A new tap replaces that day’s advice. Never dump raw errors (Safari « expected pattern », 404, model ids) in the UI.
  - `POST /api/coach-week` exists as a small fallback helper; **do not show a second coach card on Suivi**. Journal dimanche → confirmation → **Analyser dans Métabolisme**.
- **Tab 4 is the coach screen, not a second Suivi.** Weight charts, Renpho, Sunday journal, and sport routine stay on Tab 2 (no MilestoneBar). Tab 4 top: **Plan semaine** (`EnergyBalanceCard` histograms — Cible = `target_calories`, Dépense estimée = TDEE, Déficit/Surplus colored vs `primaryGoal`). Do not reuse Aujourd'hui copy (« Énergie du jour », Mangées, Brûlées). Then Faim/Motivation/Fatigue **gauges**, headline « à faire », action cards, kcal/macro deltas, selective apply. Never show BMR / TDEE labels. Flash models from live Gemini list (`lib/gemini/models.ts`). NEVER dump raw API JSON in the UI. No local mock bilan if Gemini fails — show a friendly error.
- Flexibility: Extra meals/cheats are spread over the next 3 to 4 days (-100 kcal/day adjustment).
- Tolerance: +/- 5% of daily calorie target is marked as "Goal Achieved".
- Recovery Logic: Suggest outdoor cycling or running based on habits, force rest days if high-intensity Strava workouts are detected in the last 48h.
- Qualitative Tracking: Daily **ok / bof / crevé** cat stickers (`CatSticker` / `FeelStickerRow`) on Aujourd’hui **and** the Sunday journal for **Faim / Motivation / Fatigue**. `CatSticker` is **head only** (no body, square `viewBox` 32×32) so the expression stays readable at small size: **ok** = oreilles dressées + yeux ronds + sourire ; **bof** = oreilles un peu molles + yeux en tirets + bouche plate ; **crevé** = tête penchée + oreilles tombantes + yeux en X + bouche vers le bas. `FeelStickerRow` passes `selected={on}`: face (yeux, nez, bouche) dark on the muted head; **selected in dark** → light face (`dark:fill-white` / `dark:stroke-white`) because `html.dark .bg-health-ink.text-white` paints the head `--c-on-fill` (dark on a light chip). Never a full-body silhouette. Canonical store is `CatFeelMood` (`lib/cat-feel.ts`) — Gemini and local coach read the same 3 levels (`formatFeelPromptBits`). Leftover 1–5 numbers collapse on read only (`parseFeelMood`). **clé `energy` (libellé Motivation)**. **Motivation** = pep / envie d’y aller ; **Fatigue** = corps usé / besoin de récup — they can diverge. Never rename Apple Santé « Énergie active ». Save on tap, editable later; **Réinit.** clears today's scores; **Validé** when all three are set persists `payload.checkin.validated`. Days without a note are ignored by the 7-day coach. After Validé, **Coach du jour** (`lib/today-coach.ts` `todayCoachRemark`) sits under that block. Copy = **title + advice only** — NEVER recap « Faim ok · motivation · fatigue » nor « X mangées · dépense · cible » (rings / `TodayEnergyCard` already show that). Feels drive the title; live burn from Santé (`burnedKcalFromHealth`); time of day (`parisHour` / `dayPeriod`) so evening does not count uneaten breakfast as remaining; skipped slots are never the next lever. Optional **Conseil du moment** (`POST /api/coach-today`, Flash, user tap only). Keep the 3 actions for that profile + day (`loadCoachTodayAdvice` / `persistCoachTodayAdvice`) — do not clear on snapshot change or tab switch. Hide the card until Validé. Sunday journal on Suivi still has mood / wins / blockers + the same stickers. After save, **Polaroid** 3 lines (`lib/week-polaroid.ts`, victoire / humeur / « on recommence lundi ») + CTA **Analyser dans Métabolisme** — no Gemini on save, no payload dump. Tab 4 gauges stay the Sunday journal; daily check-ins are extra 7-day signal.
- **Coach payload (Tab 2 → Tab 4):** saving a Sunday journal MUST persist `CoachWeekPayload` (`lib/coach-payload.ts`, localStorage `coach-week-payload`) containing: **7-day** weight trend (daily + MA7 + plateau flag), Sunday `journal_notes`, recent journals, **full `sport_routine`**, and profile goals. Destination `tab-4-metabolique`. Do NOT call Gemini Flash from the journal save — Tab 4 consumes the payload via **Demander l'analyse du Coach**. Show confirmation modal after save.
- **Tab 4 apply:** "Appliquer les ajustements" is **selective**. Checkboxes: **Nutrition** (default on, subtitle « Nouvelles cibles du jour · suggestions sur les repas ») writes `profils.target_*` + meal-gen bias (`coach-applied-targets`) for Tab 3; **Sport** (default on, subtitle « Ajuste durée / intensité des séances existantes. Ne crée pas de nouvelles séances. ») patches `profils.sport_routine` duration/effort — does not add sessions. Also writes `profils.applied_adjustments` (week_start Monday). After apply, a **recap that stays** on the card: cibles updated · suggestions on Aujourd'hui (logged meals not rewritten) · week plan updated / frozen if shopping fully checked / empty. Sport line if that domain was applied. Shared (duo) sessions stay in sync on both profiles.

### Tab 2 Suivi — dynamic goals & weight
- Weight goals are **per-profile** and editable (`Éditer mes objectifs`): start weight, target weight, primary goal (`perte` / `maintien` / `prise`), weekly rate.
- Persist on `profils`: `primary_goal`, `weekly_rate_kg`, `start_weight_kg`, `target_weight_kg` (also `current_weight_kg` from latest pesée).
- Weight card: open-bottom **270° arc** (`WeightJourneyChart`). Left = Départ in blue (`#5AC8FA`), right = Cible in green (`#30D158`). Fill starts on the left and turns green as progress (`progressPct`) approaches the target. Current kg in the center. **No** second 25/50/75/100% milestone bar (redundant with the arc).
- Tendance poids **and** composition corporelle ranges: **[14 jours] | [1 mois] | [3 mois] | [Tout]**. Compute MA 7j / 14j on the **full series**, then slice the window (`sliceTrendRange`). Ranges stay tied to the active profile’s pesees.
- **Screen order (per profile):** header + Éditer mes objectifs → jauge poids → **Import Renpho** (once, first profile) → **journal du dimanche** → **Journées** (déficit quotidien + retouche des repas d’un jour passé) → tendance poids → composition corporelle → Apple Santé → lien Bilan Coach → **Ma routine sport last**.

### Tab 2 — Ma routine sport (`profils.sport_routine` jsonb)
- Rendered **last** on the Suivi screen (after charts and Bilan Coach). Caption: **Ici tu construis la semaine. Aujourd’hui et Métabolisme lisent cette même routine.**
- One JSON routine per profile. Derived counters `runsPerWeek` / `ridesPerWeek` / `strengthDays` / `targetMinutesPerWeek` are recomputed from `sessions` (do not maintain a second source of truth).
- Session object (persist these keys):
  - `id`, `activity`, `effort`, `durationMin`, `elevationM` (D+ in metres), `exercises[]`, `shared`, `weekdays[]` (ISO 1=Lun … 7=Dim, multi-select).
- **Activity:** `course` | `velo` | `muscu` | `equitation` (Équitation). UI groups cards by activity.
- **Effort (by activity):** Course/Vélo: Fractionné, Sortie longue, Endurance, Récupération / Zone 2, Trail. Muscu: Circuit HIIT, Force. Équitation: Endurance, Récupération / Zone 2 (extend as needed). D+ is a **numeric target on the session**, not an effort chip.
- **Exercises:** each row has `target`: `reps` (séries × répétitions) OR `temps` (isométrie / HIIT: `workSec` effort + `restSec` repos), plus optional `notes` (consigne). Labels FR: « Répétitions / Durée », « Temps / Isométrie ». Edit via `ExerciseListEditor` (HypertrophyPlanner before apply, `SportSessionSheet` for a saved séance).
- Visual dashboard: badges for duration, D+, effort, weekdays; Éditer / Supprimer; Ajouter une séance. Session builder is a sheet (Nouvelle séance / Éditer la séance).
- **Coach Flash on the routine:** `CardioPlanner` (`POST /api/coach-cardio`) proposes course/vélo slots from prefs; user applies → writes `sport_routine.sessions`. `HypertrophyPlanner` (`POST /api/coach-hypertrophy`) only if `primaryGoal === "prise"`. Duration chips include **10 / 15 / 20 min** (availability wins). Textbook 3×45 min is a **warning**, never a lock — sessions must persist at the chosen minutes. After propose, **edit exercises in place** (name, notes/consigne, sets, reps or temps, add / remove / reorder) then **Mettre dans ma routine**. `SportSessionSheet` remains the editor for a saved séance. Copy: **Propose les séances. Tu valides → ça devient ta routine.** Both use Gemini Flash + `withGeminiWait`. Do not invent a second routine source. Tab 4 Sport **adjusts** duration/effort of existing sessions only.
- **Séance en duo (Alexis & Élodie):** toggle on the builder. `shared: true` + **same `id`** replicated on both `profils.sport_routine`. Badge **Duo**. Edit/delete of a shared session MUST prompt « Mettre à jour pour les deux profils ? » (both vs this profile only). Persist both rows in one `updateSportRoutines` write (avoid racing two catalog updates).
- Fallback: localStorage overlay if the `sport_routine` column is missing; parse must accept count-only JSON and synthesize sessions.

### Tab 2 — Sunday journal & Renpho
- Placed **just under** the weight/objectifs card (not at the bottom of Suivi).
- Sunday journal saves to `pesees.journal_notes` (JSON: mood, wins, blockers, hunger/energy/fatigue as `CatFeelMood` ok/bof/creve) on the Sunday weigh-in row. Unique `(profile_id, date)`.
- After save, `CoachReadySheet` shows a **Polaroid** (3 local lines from wins/mood + « on recommence lundi ») then **Analyser dans Métabolisme**. Do not dump `pesees.journal_notes` or the Tab 4 payload.
- History drawer title: **Historique des notes**, sorted by date desc, loaded from Supabase `journal_notes IS NOT NULL` (merge local rows).
- Renpho OCR: Gemini Flash fills the review form for the selected profile + date (merge existing `pesees` row if the day already exists). Save to `pesees` ONLY after confirm.

### Tab 2 — Journées (historique Aujourd’hui)
- After the Sunday journal, before tendance poids. This is where a past day is retouched — Aujourd’hui stays today-only.
- Daily net = mangées − brûlées Santé (`lib/energy-history.ts` `buildDailyEnergy` + `lib/energy-balance.ts`). Same sign / color vs `primaryGoal` as `TodayEnergyCard`.
- `RangeToggle` **[14 jours] | [1 mois] | [3 mois] | [Tout]**. Chart = days with meals **or** live Santé (no fake TDEE deficit on empty days). List always includes at least the last 14 calendar days so yesterday is tappable.
- Tap a day → `DayLogSheet`: résumé (Mangées / Brûlées / déficit + `CompactMacrosRow`) + Faim/Motivation/Fatigue if a check-in exists (read-only) + 4 meal slots. Skip / empty slot insert. Edit grams via `EditMealSheet`. Persist `upsertMeal` / `fetchMealsRange` with that ISO `date`.
- Do **not** duplicate Séance du jour or Activité here — those stay on Aujourd’hui + the Apple Santé block. No second coach card.

---

## 6. CODE ARCHITECTURE
- Step-by-Step Generation: Build modularly (DB -> UI -> Features -> APIs).
- State Management: Use robust React state and `window.storage` for persistence.
- Zero Regression: Do not break existing UI when adding features. Ask for confirmation before refactoring.
- Dates: Europe/Paris (`lib/dates.ts`). Seed today + yesterday meals if today’s `repas` is empty.
- Data model (filter by `profile_id`, not Auth uid):
  - `profils`: `primary_goal`, `weekly_rate_kg`, `start_weight_kg`, `target_weight_kg`, `current_weight_kg`, **`sport_routine` jsonb**, **`meal_templates` jsonb**, `target_calories`, `target_protein_g`, `target_carbs_g`, `target_fat_g`, **`applied_adjustments` jsonb**.
  - `sport_routine` shape: `{ runsPerWeek, ridesPerWeek, strengthDays, targetMinutesPerWeek, sessions: [{ id, activity, effort, durationMin, elevationM, shared, weekdays, exercises: [{ id, name, sets, target, reps, workSec, restSec, notes? }] }] }`.
  - `repas` (incl. `is_skipped`). `MealEntry.date` optional ISO; `insertMeal` writes it when valid, else `todayISO()`. `fetchMealsRange` loads a profile’s days for Suivi Journées.
  - `logs_sante` (workouts may be `source=manual` from Tab 1), `parametres` (single `foyer` row, **`favorite_recipes` jsonb**, **`rejected_recipes` jsonb**, **`pantry_stock` jsonb**), `plans_semaine` (one JSON plan per Monday, **`lunch_dessert`** + **`dinner_dessert` jsonb**).
  - `pesees`: weight / body comp / Sunday **`journal_notes`**; unique `(profile_id, date)`.
- Tab 1 architecture: meals + Faim/Motivation/Fatigue (then **Coach du jour** if Validé — advice only, optional **Conseil du moment** (3 actions stay for the Paris day via `coach-today-advice:{profileId}:{date}`)) + **Séance du jour** from the selected profile’s `sport_routine` + weekday; **Modifier / Noter une séance faite** (`lib/today-sport.ts`) without rewriting the routine (**Modifier does not auto-Validé**; overlay ≠ done); course/vélo title **Dénivelé** not Endurance; Santé/Strava match via `lib/strava-match.ts` `matchWorkoutsToPlanned`; unmatched rows **C’est ça** (Validé); pill **À faire / Validé** is tappable (manual, `dismissed` blocks re-match, works after Modifier). No « Simuler sync Strava ». **Couple** meal writes hit both profiles (`upsertMeal`). **Dupliquer** copies a filled slot to the other profile when theirs is empty (lunch/dinner caption « Tu lui copies le tien ? »). Lunch/dinner **plat** auto-fills from this week’s `plans_semaine` (`lib/serve-week-plan.ts`, 1 portion) when the slot is empty, dessert-only, or a demo seed — never overwrite a logged plat; button **Mettre le plat de la semaine** to replace plat only (`withKeptDessert`). **Échanger avec un plat de la semaine** (`MoveMealSheet` + `moveMealInPlan`) swaps today’s lunch/dinner slot with another filled week slot, then force-serves today for both profiles. **Heart** (`FavoriteHeart`) and **Ban** (`RejectMealButton`) on déjeuner/dîner when `canFavoriteMeal(weekDish)` — full `PlannedMeal` snapshot for favorites; rejected is title/theme only (`lib/rejected.ts`). Same title re-heart updates the favorite. Ban and heart are exclusive. No heart/ban on PD / collation / dessert-only logs. Reset = `applyTodaySlotTemplates` from Paramètres DB (`replacePlan` + `force`), no mock bowls / no localStorage planned overlay. Desserts live on the same `dejeuner` / `diner` row (`Dessert :` prefix); cards show name + kcal + protein + dessert grams (ingredients only in `EditMealSheet`). `fillMissingSlotsFromTemplates` / `applyTodaySlotTemplates` merge dessert templates from `profils.meal_templates` (and local overlay). Coach ingredient adds skip dessert lines (`lib/coach-ingredients.ts`). Applied coach diffs (`profils.applied_adjustments` jsonb, week-scoped) show coral **Ajustement Coach** badges. Nutrition badges translate daily macro deltas into **concrete ingredient adds**: staple **Idéal** and **Rapide** are rule-based (next prep / pantry). **Never auto-call Gemini** on tab open or meal tap. **Autre idée** = Gemini **Flash** `POST /api/coach-quick-add` fitted to **that** dish (no-prep, diet, aversions, avoid list). Fallback pantry list if Flash fails. Do not rewrite overnight-oats grams on Today. Week plan / shopping still boosts the staple on remaining days. Sport: duration tags; dismiss via the badge X (or auto-hide a séance once Validé). Rings / macros / meal kcal use `lib/macro-status.ts` vs `primaryGoal`: green when on-track or helping (kcal under for perte, protein ≥95%), red when off-goal (kcal over for perte, under for prise). Tolerance ±5% kcal = achieved. Edit-meal sheet **Ajouter au plat** = 4 saisie rapide modes (incl. **Récents**); skip slot picker; keep dessert lines. Photo: **Appareil photo** vs **Photothèque** (`ImagePickButton`, input not `display:none`). Barcode: same two buttons; grams and kcal independent (`macrosAtGramsWithCalories`). Qty/grams/kcal on `QtyEditRow` (compact one-band row, Today + Paramètres PD/collation). `TodayEnergyCard` on the dashboard. Activité tiles: Pas / Marche / Vélo / Exercice / **Active** / Repos — never **Hors sport**. Logging: `POST /api/log-text`, `POST /api/log-photo` (Flash) behind `withGeminiWait`. **Récents** = 14 j, last grammage, save immédiat (include desserts; skip plat of `source === "plan"` only). **Comme hier** on PD + collation (vide ou template). Time-of-day CTA later, but **evening can still complete lunch** if it was not logged at noon.
- Tab 2 architecture: pesees load/save (`lib/supabase/pesees.ts`); goals (`saveProfileGoals`) + sport (`saveSportRoutines`); journal history `loadJournalHistory`; coach payload `lib/coach-payload.ts` (7-day window). Weight arc `WeightJourneyChart` (open bottom, blue→green). **Journées** (`DayEnergyCard` + `DayLogSheet`): repas range + Santé → déficit quotidien (mangées − brûlées), `RangeToggle` 14j / 1m / 3m / Tout, tap a day to retouch meals (`upsertMeal` with that `date`, never `todayISO()` on insert of a past day). Screen order: objectifs + arc → Renpho → journal → **Journées** → tendance → composition → Apple Santé → bilan Coach → **routine sport last** (`SportRoutineCard` + `CardioPlanner` / `HypertrophyPlanner` if prise). Hypertrophy proposal is **editable in place** (`ExerciseListEditor`) before apply; saved muscu cards list each exercise + notes. Body-comp and weight charts share `RangeToggle` / `sliceTrendRange`.
- Tab 3 architecture: weekly plan UI + **Dessert · cette semaine** (`DessertBatchCard`, Midi | Soir light, persist `plans_semaine.lunch_dessert` / `dinner_dessert`, optional pack photo `POST /api/dessert-product`, `repairDessertIntegrity` + `scaleDessertToGoals` so both profiles share the same dessert and perte never gets more maple/nuts/chocolate; **Ingrédient** swap light-first on the dessert sheet) + **En stock** (`StockPanel`) + `GenerateControls` **Pistes du moment** (`lib/meal-inspo.ts` `pickMealInspirations` — saison / météo / prefs / aversions / stock / Plus jamais ; tap → thème ; **Autres pistes** local ; **never** Gemini on tab open) + `POST /api/generate-meals` (Gemini Pro, `maxDuration` 300, wait overlay); `annotatePlan` → `expandPreparedSauces` (`lib/homemade-sauces.ts`) so loaded weeks explode jar sauces; shopping from `lib/shopping-from-plan.ts` (`shoppingDisplayName` merge + aisle fold `œ`→`oe`); Batch Master Plan from `lib/batch-from-plan.ts` (`buildBatchSession`) — packing = **Boîte Alexis / Boîte Élodie** + pot sauce, grams = 1 repas; section **3. Sauces** = stacked ingredients + qty (`stackedSauceLines`, no TM column, no mix steps). Recipe chrome `RecipeTag` / `lib/plan-colors.ts` / `lib/ingredient-groups.ts` / `HoldTip`. On-screen guide + PDF share the same session object. Never invent a second week source — always the selected `week_start`. Pass **meal coach** (`lib/meal-coach.ts` from `profils.primary_goal` + `target_*` + dessert templates) so Gem Chef uses **per-profile** lunch/dinner kcal (dessert templates already subtracted) and `grams_alexis` / `grams_elodie` (same dish, different portions except sauces/vinaigrettes which stay shared; perte = veg volume, prise = starch/protein density; protein never cut). Do NOT put desserts in Gem Chef recipes. Server `scalePlanToGoals` is the safety net if Gemini equalizes grams. Also pass applied Tab 4 bias (`loadHouseholdCoachBias`) so next-week generation respects applied coach targets. Pass **stock** (`formatStockForPrompt`) when the foyer toggle is on. After generate, consume matched pantry items. Active-week nutrition deltas also bump remaining plan grams + shopping extras (`lib/coach-plan-sync.ts`) **only if** the week’s shopping list is not fully checked. **Banner** if current targets/goals differ from the stamp saved at last generate / quantity update (`lib/plan-targets.ts`): *Cibles changées* → **Mettre à jour les quantités** (`scalePlanToGoals`, same recipes, no Gemini). **Plus tard** acknowledges until the next change. Empty week = no banner. **Favoris** (4th sub-tab): **Favoris | Plus jamais**. Household lists from Today lunch/dinner marks **and** the recipe sheet on Repas (`FavoriteHeart` / `RejectMealButton` on `RecipeDetailSheet`). Favoris: `lib/favorites.ts`, `parametres.favorite_recipes`. Plus jamais: `lib/rejected.ts`, `parametres.rejected_recipes` — Gem Chef + today-swap never regenerate those titles (`mergeAvoidTitles` into `pastMeals`); list is editable (title/theme, add by text, **Je change d’avis**). Ban does not delete the current week slot. Group by theme, search title/theme/ingredients. Open sheet: edit title/theme, Retirer, **Mettre dans la semaine** → `placeRecipeInSlots` + `scalePlanToGoals` (Lun–Ven = both batch pair slots). Same title re-heart updates the snapshot. No Gemini. Deep retouch = place on the week then existing swap/regen, then re-heart.
- Tab 4 architecture: `EnergyBalanceCard` (top) + `CoachAnalysisCard` + `POST /api/coach-analysis` (Gemini Flash) with 7-day Santé activity (`fetchActivityRange`); apply via selected domains → `updateTargets` (`profils.target_*` + `coach-applied-targets`) and/or `updateSportRoutines` (`sport_routine` duration/effort).
- Tab 5 architecture: `ParametresScreen`. (1) **Règles à respecter** : chips exclusifs `recipePace` + `heatStyle`, toggles foyer (tofu, simili, dîners low cal, météo, sauces maison), `extraRules` tags (+ critère libre). Aversions par profil. Matériel. `persistKitchenPrefs` → `parametres` (`kitchen_prefs` jsonb) + local `lib/kitchen-prefs.ts`. Gem Chef reads `formatKitchenPrefsForPrompt`. (2) **Petit-déj, collations & desserts** : `profils.meal_templates` (`lib/meal-templates.ts`) par profil, jours ISO comme `sport_routine`. Types : `petit-dejeuner` | `collation` | `dessert-midi` | `dessert-soir`. Tab 1 auto-remplit PD/collation vides ; desserts merge into `dejeuner` / `diner` (even logged meals if no `Dessert :` lines yet; skip if `Dessert : —` or dessert already present). Saving templates calls `applyTodaySlotTemplates(..., { replacePlan: true })`. **Never** replace saved `meal_templates` with `defaultMealTemplates` (skyr / oats démo) — defaults only if the column is null. (3) Connexions: `GET /api/connections` (booleans only, never secrets) + masked localStorage `api-keys`. Strava copy: **pas d’API live gratuite** depuis 2026-06-30 — séances via Apple Santé + Raccourci ; token API optionnel seulement si abo Strava (Premium, pas de frais développeur en plus). Webhook URL `{origin}/api/webhooks/health` (`?profile_id=alexis|elodie`, alias `/api/health-webhook`; GET + POST). Ingest → `logs_sante` (`kind=activite`, source `apple_health`) then Tab 1 Activité. (4) Thème: `useTheme().setScheme` (same as top-bar Moon/Sun). CTA **Enregistrer les préférences** + toast. PAS de routine sport / objectifs ici (Suivi).
- Theme: `ThemeProvider` wraps the app; CSS variables + `html.dark` overrides for `bg-white` surfaces and `bg-health-ink text-white` fills. `data-season` / `data-weather` on `<html>` tint `--c-bg` in light only (dark stays `#000`). Live weather chip in the top bar (`WeatherChip`, Eschentzwiller — icône + °, no sky word). Tap → 7-day sheet via `createPortal(document.body)` (never inside the sticky/`backdrop-blur` header). Croix + tap overlay to close. No season silhouettes.
- Dev RLS: open `anon` + `authenticated` (`using (true)`). Tighten when household Auth lands.
- Code Quality: Keep components clean, without missing brackets, using realistic mock data for initial setup. Keep all secrets in `.env.local` (Supabase URLs, Webhook endpoints, Gemini API keys).
